// Title: Headless Process Launched Via Conhost.EXE
// Sigma ID: 00ca75ab-d5ce-43be-b86c-55ff39c6abfc
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-07-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.001, T1059.003
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects the launch of a child process via "conhost.exe" with the "--headless" flag. The "--
//   headless" flag hides the windows from the user upon execution.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.huntress.com/blog/fake-browser-updates-lead-to-boinc-volunteer-computing-software
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_conhost_headless_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\conhost.exe" and InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains "--headless"
